- Grouping up!

263
00:20:02,090 --> 00:20:03,600
In the same bush, yeah.

264
00:20:05,710 --> 00:20:08,510
- Preaw, go bait them.
- Hold on, wait.

265
00:20:08,540 --> 00:20:09,670
Just like that.

266
00:20:09,790 --> 00:20:11,010
Someone's coming.

267
00:20:11,040 --> 00:20:13,850
- Go, go, go! This is it.
- Alright, let's hit it!

268
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:19,440
(The Red Team's tower
has been destroyed)

269
00:20:24,700 --> 00:20:26,150
- Whoa...
- That's it!

270
00:20:28,800 --> 00:20:30,460
Hell yeah! Keep those wins coming.

271
00:20:36,150 --> 00:20:38,140
And at this match point
for B.S. Brothers,

272
00:20:38,160 --> 00:20:41,690
will they end
Apex Sharkz's run right here?

273
00:20:41,750 --> 00:20:43,420
They're playing so cracked.

274
00:20:43,440 --> 00:20:45,360
- Chill out.
- Sorry. My bad.

275
00:20:45,490 --> 00:20:48,400
And now, they just need to
finish the objectives.

276
00:20:48,430 --> 00:20:50,820
Just finish the base 'cause winning
means taking down the base, kids!

277
00:20:51,030 --> 00:20:52,670
- Get in there!
- Yeah.

278
00:20:52,840 --> 00:20:54,320
(The Red Team's tower has been destroyed)
Keep pushing.

279
00:20:58,810 --> 00:20:59,630
Now what?

280
00:21:04,060 --> 00:21:04,820
And now,

281
00:21:04,840 --> 00:21:08,490
the team moving on to face
the loser of the upper bracket tomorrow

282
00:21:08,630 --> 00:21:09,920
is...

283
00:21:10,210 --> 00:21:12,910
- B.S. Brothers!
- B.S. Brothers!

284
00:21:15,380 --> 00:21:16,860
B.S. Brothers, baby!

285
00:21:17,520 --> 00:21:18,570
B.S. Brothers!

286
00:21:24,570 --> 00:21:25,170
What the hell?

287
00:21:25,180 --> 00:21:26,170
Damn it!

288
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:27,950
Play like we practiced!

289
00:21:27,970 --> 00:21:30,770
- Just play the way we practiced!
- No, you said don't go too far.

290
00:21:30,790 --> 00:21:31,890
F*ck!

291
00:21:33,350 --> 00:21:35,270
Sh*t, they're real dark horses.

292
00:21:35,370 --> 00:21:36,360
How did that happen?

293
00:21:36,700 --> 00:21:39,760
Look, even if they qualify,
they're not gonna make it anyway.

294
00:21:40,570 --> 00:21:42,200
They've finally made it!

295
00:21:42,220 --> 00:21:43,300
This is the ultimate dark horse team

296
00:21:43,330 --> 00:21:46,400
in the RoV Pro League 2026 Summer!

297
00:21:46,420 --> 00:21:47,440
That's incredible.

298
00:21:48,130 --> 00:21:51,040
After being looked down upon
for several seasons

299
00:21:51,060 --> 00:21:52,380
and consistently being out of form,

300
00:21:52,430 --> 00:21:54,800
people thought they were finished.

301
00:21:54,860 --> 00:21:56,490
But they've made a comeback!

302
00:21:56,520 --> 00:21:59,390
Like I always say, the comeback is real.

303
00:21:59,410 --> 00:22:01,390
This is B.S. Brothers!

304
00:22:05,300 --> 00:22:06,200
Be careful.

305
00:22:06,910 --> 00:22:07,720
Come on.

306
00:22:08,050 --> 00:22:09,940
One, two, three!

307
00:22:15,480 --> 00:22:17,450
Man, I only made it because of you guys.

308
00:22:17,460 --> 00:22:18,520
Thanks for carrying me.

309
00:22:18,530 --> 00:22:20,680
Hey, what are you talking about?
We didn't do that.

310
00:22:20,700 --> 00:22:24,030
Yeah, we won because of teamwork.

311
00:22:25,300 --> 00:22:26,150
- Exactly.
- Hey.

312
00:22:26,920 --> 00:22:28,620
No one's carrying anyone here.

313
00:22:28,650 --> 00:22:30,460
We just have each other's backs.

314
00:22:33,350 --> 00:22:35,180
Great job, Captain.

315
00:22:41,210 --> 00:22:42,020
Thank you.

316
00:22:43,090 --> 00:22:44,780
Thank you so much
for choosing to stand by me.

317
00:22:45,770 --> 00:22:47,410
P'Three, you're everything to me.

318
00:22:49,770 --> 00:22:50,680
Just hug each other.

319
00:22:50,830 --> 00:22:52,150
We won!

320
00:22:52,850 --> 00:22:55,160
- Go, go, go!
- Let's dance.

321
00:22:56,020 --> 00:22:57,760
- They're not joining us.
- Come on.

322
00:22:57,780 --> 00:22:58,660
- To the right.
- Let's go.

323
00:22:58,680 --> 00:23:00,400
To the left. Now, to the right.

324
00:23:06,080 --> 00:23:08,000
That was insane.

325
00:23:09,230 --> 00:23:10,740
You've got some serious luck.

326
00:23:12,470 --> 00:23:13,930
More luck than skill, obviously.

327
00:23:15,330 --> 00:23:17,480
I really have to hand it
to your trash-talking skills, Ten.

328
00:23:17,500 --> 00:23:19,200
Say whatever the hell you want

329
00:23:20,140 --> 00:23:22,210
because the person
you're trying to use as my weakness

330
00:23:25,830 --> 00:23:27,570
is actually my greatest strength.

331
00:23:59,350 --> 00:24:01,770
(And for Blue Viper's results,)

332
00:24:01,840 --> 00:24:04,430
(the MVP award goes to Peem.)

333
00:24:04,460 --> 00:24:08,210
(Whoa, well deserved for THE PEEM.)

334
00:24:08,230 --> 00:24:11,700
(He carried the team so hard.
Not sure if that wore him out.)

335
00:24:11,730 --> 00:24:14,200
(The MVP,
or the Most Valuable Player...)

336
00:24:41,450 --> 00:24:42,180
Wait.

337
00:24:42,760 --> 00:24:43,810
Stay with me for a bit.

338
00:25:04,860 --> 00:25:07,460
Thought we were gonna be strangers
until the tournament ends?

339
00:25:08,890 --> 00:25:11,920
What kind of strangers smoke together?

340
00:25:13,640 --> 00:25:16,060
Can't strangers just smoke
in the same spot?

341
00:25:20,440 --> 00:25:21,880
Your playstyle
was annoying as hell today.

342
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:25,920
So annoying that I don't even
want to see your face anymore.

343
00:25:27,560 --> 00:25:29,480
Well, you're free to keep being annoyed.

344
00:25:30,170 --> 00:25:31,150
Tomorrow's the final.

345
00:25:31,680 --> 00:25:33,600
Get ready to face my team.

346
00:25:36,700 --> 00:25:38,490
I really want to put you in your place

347
00:25:39,530 --> 00:25:41,180
and snuff out your confidence
just like this cigarette.

348
00:25:48,020 --> 00:25:48,770
Ten...

349
00:25:58,870 --> 00:26:00,460
You can give it back to me
after the final.

350
00:26:22,850 --> 00:26:24,550
Dive in, dive in!

351
00:26:24,570 --> 00:26:26,780
- Play the lanes.
- This is easy.

352
00:26:39,290 --> 00:26:41,620
- You shouldn't have died just now.
- Yeah, focus.

353
00:26:41,640 --> 00:26:42,360
Yeah.

354
00:26:42,660 --> 00:26:43,850
Don't lose your mind just yet.

355
00:26:51,080 --> 00:26:53,870
- Jay, call the play!
- Hey, help me out over here.

356
00:26:53,900 --> 00:26:55,160
P'Jay, open the map.

357
00:26:55,330 --> 00:26:56,230
Dammit.

358
00:27:01,450 --> 00:27:03,030
- Push, push!
- Go!

359
00:27:06,680 --> 00:27:09,300
Wait, wait for the power spike.
Don't go in just to die.

360
00:27:09,320 --> 00:27:11,810
- Fall back, then!
- Don't go out and feed.

361
00:27:11,830 --> 00:27:13,410
- Get out!
- Pull back!

362
00:27:22,590 --> 00:27:23,670
I told you so.

363
00:27:35,030 --> 00:27:36,280
What a waste.

364
00:27:36,530 --> 00:27:37,660
- This sucks.
- Yeah.

365
00:27:37,730 --> 00:27:38,500
This is so frustrating.

366
00:27:39,370 --> 00:27:40,270
- Damn...
- Forget it.

367
00:27:40,380 --> 00:27:41,930
We gave it our all, didn't we?

368
00:27:41,980 --> 00:27:43,050
Third place isn't that bad.

369
00:27:44,280 --> 00:27:45,920
They're really cracked this year.

370
00:27:45,950 --> 00:27:46,770
I mean...

371
00:27:47,600 --> 00:27:48,550
Let's try again next year.

372
00:27:49,050 --> 00:27:50,000
Hey, but I think...

373
00:27:50,570 --> 00:27:51,570
Stop right there.

374
00:27:53,020 --> 00:27:54,600
I'm already losing my mind as it is.

375
00:27:58,650 --> 00:27:59,280
Hey.

376
00:27:59,790 --> 00:28:01,600
Guess you're not just
a "bullsh*t" team anymore.

377
00:28:02,180 --> 00:28:03,320
Go and take that championship,

378
00:28:03,510 --> 00:28:04,630
B.S. Brothers.

379
00:28:05,950 --> 00:28:07,480
- See you.
- See ya.

380
00:29:06,710 --> 00:29:09,470
From this angle,
the stage is pretty grand, isn't it?

381
00:29:10,850 --> 00:29:12,190
If we get to stand up there,

382
00:29:12,590 --> 00:29:14,250
it would be so cool.

383
00:29:19,490 --> 00:29:21,970
I finally managed to make it up there,

384
00:29:22,920 --> 00:29:26,130
but in the end,
they still didn't come to see me.

385
00:29:27,870 --> 00:29:30,680
I know I've had
such a big ego in the past

386
00:29:30,790 --> 00:29:32,270
to make a stand against my family

387
00:29:32,490 --> 00:29:35,800
that I wouldn't show my face
until I succeeded.

388
00:29:36,050 --> 00:29:37,250
But now that I'm actually here,

389
00:29:37,970 --> 00:29:40,120
I don't want to wait until I succeed
just to show off anymore.

390
00:29:41,030 --> 00:29:43,390
I already invited them,
but they didn't want to come.

391
00:29:44,070 --> 00:29:45,560
I just want them to see

392
00:29:45,650 --> 00:29:47,840
how much effort
I've put in along the way.

393
00:29:58,190 --> 00:29:59,600
Just wait a little longer, P'Three.

394
00:30:00,480 --> 00:30:02,630
I'll help you take that trophy home
to show your family.

395
00:30:06,730 --> 00:30:07,970
When that time comes,

396
00:30:08,730 --> 00:30:09,830
I believe...

397
00:30:10,160 --> 00:30:11,680
that they'll be proud

398
00:30:12,030 --> 00:30:14,230
to have a son who is this talented
and hardworking.

399
00:30:14,340 --> 00:30:15,300
Oh, please.

400
00:30:15,530 --> 00:30:18,980
Wow, you're really fired up.

401
00:30:19,000 --> 00:30:20,920
Where are you getting
all this confidence from?

402
00:30:20,930 --> 00:30:22,660
Ow, P'Three!

403
00:30:23,030 --> 00:30:24,880
You're pinching my cheeks way too hard.

404
00:30:28,060 --> 00:30:29,040
Thanks, Soh.

405
00:30:31,630 --> 00:30:34,940
Even if we don't win the trophy,

406
00:30:35,810 --> 00:30:37,200
I've got a reward just for you.

407
00:30:38,680 --> 00:30:42,380
And you think you're the only one
who has a surprise?

408
00:30:42,450 --> 00:30:43,130
Whoa.

409
00:30:44,320 --> 00:30:45,500
Are you surprising me back?

410
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:48,240
Or are you just throwing
my own words back at me?

411
00:30:49,830 --> 00:30:52,070
Hey, you're ignoring me?

412
00:30:52,100 --> 00:30:54,310
Soh, what is it?
What are you giving me?

413
00:30:55,030 --> 00:30:56,630
What is it? A microwave?

414
00:31:06,130 --> 00:31:07,130
Where did everyone go?

415
00:31:11,370 --> 00:31:13,150
Your voice got here before you did.

416
00:31:13,300 --> 00:31:16,290
A quick walk after that meal
made me feel much better.

417
00:31:16,320 --> 00:31:16,840
Jeez.

418
00:31:18,770 --> 00:31:22,000
- Keep those eyes wide open, though.
- Exactly.

419
00:31:22,030 --> 00:31:24,130
- Come on, cheer up!
- Cheer up.

420
00:31:24,550 --> 00:31:26,490
The match is in 40 minutes, guys.

421
00:31:27,930 --> 00:31:29,160
Come on, guys.

422
00:31:29,940 --> 00:31:31,320
- Here we go.
- Let's go.

423
00:31:31,410 --> 00:31:32,080
Alright.

424
00:31:33,800 --> 00:31:34,680
- Ready.
- Yeah.

425
00:31:35,330 --> 00:31:35,960
Wait.

426
00:31:37,780 --> 00:31:38,750
What are you looking for?

427
00:31:39,970 --> 00:31:41,230
My bear head.

428
00:31:41,540 --> 00:31:42,880
Where's my bear head?

429
00:31:45,270 --> 00:31:47,320
Look for it, guys. Hurry.

430
00:31:48,040 --> 00:31:49,120
Move it, look around.

431
00:31:49,490 --> 00:31:50,430
Did you check over there?

432
00:31:56,290 --> 00:31:57,190
P'Jack, found it?

433
00:31:57,280 --> 00:31:58,120
No.

434
00:31:58,280 --> 00:31:59,160
It's Ten, that bastard.

435
00:32:00,770 --> 00:32:02,290
- Hey! Three!
- Three!

436
00:32:02,310 --> 00:32:04,030
- Come on, follow him.
- P'Three!

437
00:32:13,610 --> 00:32:14,980
- Ten, you bastard!
- Three!

438
00:32:15,120 --> 00:32:16,370
Where did you put the bear head?

439
00:32:17,430 --> 00:32:18,710
What the hell is wrong with you?

440
00:32:19,920 --> 00:32:21,610
Can you drop
the sh*tty attitude for once

441
00:32:21,630 --> 00:32:23,240
and just follow the rules?

442
00:32:23,270 --> 00:32:25,090
Is that too hard
for your tiny brain to handle?

443
00:32:25,110 --> 00:32:26,790
Why don't you take a good look
at yourself first?

444
00:32:26,840 --> 00:32:28,210
Barging into another team's room,

445
00:32:28,230 --> 00:32:29,910
you call that following the rules?

446
00:32:30,260 --> 00:32:31,390
And what about back then?

447
00:32:31,520 --> 00:32:33,320
You sold your own team's strategies
to the rivals.

448
00:32:33,450 --> 00:32:34,880
Do you call that following the rules?

449
00:32:35,790 --> 00:32:36,560
That's enough.

450
00:33:04,810 --> 00:33:07,860
I'll radio the security guards
at the different posts for you,

451
00:33:07,880 --> 00:33:09,250
but I have to be honest...

452
00:33:09,530 --> 00:33:12,200
With this many people
and so little time left,

453
00:33:12,240 --> 00:33:15,060
I think you'd better get ready
for the match instead.

454
00:33:15,540 --> 00:33:18,640
In that case, can I ask
to delay the match just a little bit?

455
00:33:19,860 --> 00:33:21,160
I'll coordinate that for you,

456
00:33:21,190 --> 00:33:23,500
but there's only so much
we can delay it.

457
00:33:23,530 --> 00:33:25,210
Otherwise, it'll throw off
the entire schedule.

458
00:33:25,510 --> 00:33:27,550
Got it. I understand.
Thank you very much.

459
00:33:49,310 --> 00:33:50,480
Don't worry, Soh.

460
00:33:50,990 --> 00:33:52,260
I've bought us some time.

461
00:33:53,550 --> 00:33:55,400
Everyone's looking for it right now.

462
00:33:56,100 --> 00:33:57,120
We'll find it soon.

463
00:34:01,300 --> 00:34:02,990
And what if we don't?

464
00:34:04,330 --> 00:34:05,770
If I don't have that bear head,

465
00:34:07,000 --> 00:34:08,600
I definitely won't be able to play.

466
00:34:10,590 --> 00:34:14,000
What if I lose my focus
and cost the team the match?

467
00:34:20,130 --> 00:34:22,520
You've worked so hard
to get to this point.

468
00:34:23,770 --> 00:34:25,600
What if it's all ruined because of me?

469
00:34:33,980 --> 00:34:35,720
Proving myself to my family

470
00:34:36,870 --> 00:34:38,160
does matter to me,

471
00:34:38,840 --> 00:34:40,480
but what matters most right now

472
00:34:41,490 --> 00:34:42,840
isn't that anymore.

473
00:34:45,750 --> 00:34:47,290
It's about how you feel.

474
00:34:54,850 --> 00:34:56,670
Now, my boy.

475
00:34:57,200 --> 00:34:59,090
What did you just tell me?

476
00:34:59,890 --> 00:35:01,280
No matter what happens,

477
00:35:02,240 --> 00:35:03,520
we'll get through it together.

478
00:35:08,490 --> 00:35:10,520
I'm only standing here today
because of you.

479
00:35:12,750 --> 00:35:13,640
So...

480
00:35:15,230 --> 00:35:16,100
today,

481
00:35:18,380 --> 00:35:20,120
you're going to get through this, too.

482
00:35:24,510 --> 00:35:25,640
Up there on stage...

483
00:35:26,150 --> 00:35:27,580
with me standing beside you,

484
00:35:27,870 --> 00:35:30,210
it's safer than having the bear head on.

485
00:35:32,070 --> 00:35:32,960
Or...

486
00:35:33,790 --> 00:35:36,960
want to use my muscles
to shield your face?

487
00:35:52,010 --> 00:35:54,010
Alright, everyone. Welcome...

488
00:35:54,030 --> 00:35:57,970
to the RoV Pro League 2026 Summer.

489
00:35:58,000 --> 00:36:01,260
- And this is the Grand Final!
- The Grand Final!

490
00:36:06,580 --> 00:36:07,860
Whoa, my apologies.

491
00:36:07,890 --> 00:36:09,470
There's been a slight delay
in the match,

492
00:36:09,490 --> 00:36:12,240
but the excitement is guaranteed
to be worth it.

493
00:36:12,890 --> 00:36:14,330
It always has to be us, huh?

494
00:36:14,360 --> 00:36:16,240
Somehow, trouble always finds us.

495
00:36:16,440 --> 00:36:18,800
Even though the schedule
has been pushed back,

496
00:36:18,820 --> 00:36:20,240
the action is exactly as promised.

497
00:36:20,260 --> 00:36:22,480
We're ready to serve up the fun to you.

498
00:36:22,510 --> 00:36:23,920
But right now, the fans...

499
00:36:23,950 --> 00:36:25,310
Wait, I can barely hear the crowd.

500
00:36:25,330 --> 00:36:27,520
Hello? Let's hear some noise
from the crowd!

501
00:36:27,550 --> 00:36:29,750
We're about to head into
the Grand Final.

502
00:36:29,770 --> 00:36:31,620
Make some noise!

503
00:36:33,920 --> 00:36:36,080
Here is the moment
you've been waiting for.

504
00:36:36,100 --> 00:36:37,940
It's time for the Grand Final.

505
00:36:37,970 --> 00:36:42,520
RPL Summer 2026 is about to kick off!

506
00:37:00,930 --> 00:37:03,090
Alright, now, let's meet...

507
00:37:03,110 --> 00:37:05,080
the final two teams
heading into the Grand Final:

508
00:37:05,110 --> 00:37:08,240
Blue Viper and B.S. Brothers!

509
00:37:26,910 --> 00:37:28,560
Wait, hold on a second.

510
00:37:28,660 --> 00:37:30,720
Is that Soh, Derya MK12?

511
00:37:32,030 --> 00:37:33,710
Whoa, Soh is doing a face reveal!

512
00:37:33,980 --> 00:37:36,000
Damn, revealing it now?
He must be dead serious.

513
00:37:36,280 --> 00:37:38,560
But why does he look so pale?

514
00:37:38,990 --> 00:37:40,180
A face reveal?

515
00:37:40,210 --> 00:37:41,720
Will he be able to focus?

516
00:37:41,840 --> 00:37:42,910
- I know, right?
- Yeah.

517
00:37:43,030 --> 00:37:43,880
Sh*t...

518
00:38:46,980 --> 00:38:47,710
Come on.

519
00:38:53,260 --> 00:38:53,940
Let's do it.

520
00:39:01,190 --> 00:39:01,870
Guys...

521
00:39:11,030 --> 00:39:13,390
This is the moment
everyone's been waiting for.

522
00:39:13,410 --> 00:39:16,480
The overlooked dark horse,
B.S. Brothers,

523
00:39:16,550 --> 00:39:20,240
has successfully made it to face
the defending champion, Blue Viper.

524
00:39:24,640 --> 00:39:27,160
Keep an eye on the key players
from both teams.

525
00:39:27,190 --> 00:39:29,840
It'll be either Three or Ten
rising to the top

526
00:39:29,870 --> 00:39:33,280
of the RPL Summer 2026 tonight.

527
00:39:33,300 --> 00:39:37,720
Without further ado, let's get into it!

528
00:39:40,910 --> 00:39:42,670
(Welcome to Arena of Valor)

529
00:39:50,310 --> 00:39:51,670
- Dive in!
- Got it.

530
00:39:52,550 --> 00:39:53,530
Just push forward.

531
00:40:00,890 --> 00:40:01,960
Soh, look out!

532
00:40:02,160 --> 00:40:03,410
Soh! Soh...

533
00:40:16,430 --> 00:40:17,810
- Clean play!
- Nice.

534
00:40:17,840 --> 00:40:19,820
- Great.
- They suck.

535
00:40:20,270 --> 00:40:21,280
It's okay, Soh.

536
00:40:21,690 --> 00:40:22,510
Just reset.

537
00:40:24,260 --> 00:40:25,360
Let's try again.

538
00:40:26,680 --> 00:40:28,870
Soh, calm down, bro.

539
00:40:35,130 --> 00:40:37,570
- Get him. He's being so cocky.
- Almost there.

540
00:40:37,690 --> 00:40:39,630
Combo! Combo!

541
00:40:50,500 --> 00:40:53,690
(Seriously? Is this the same Derya
in the bear head?)

542
00:40:53,770 --> 00:40:56,320
(Too many conditions.
Get a new Support next season.)

543
00:40:56,340 --> 00:40:57,130
(For real.)

544
00:40:57,160 --> 00:40:59,850
(Ugh, B.S. Brothers...
They're losing because of the Support.)

545
00:41:01,490 --> 00:41:02,750
Can you hear me, Soh?

546
00:41:08,680 --> 00:41:09,330
Soh!

547
00:41:12,860 --> 00:41:14,400
Remember what I told you?

548
00:41:27,400 --> 00:41:29,520
If you're still scared
once you're up on that stage,

549
00:41:33,590 --> 00:41:34,760
then don't look at them.

550
00:41:36,120 --> 00:41:38,760
Just think of it
as if no one is watching us.

551
00:41:39,270 --> 00:41:42,410
We're just sitting comfortably

552
00:41:43,160 --> 00:41:46,010
in our most comfortable spot.

553
00:41:57,890 --> 00:41:59,230
If you still feel unsure,

554
00:41:59,950 --> 00:42:00,990
then look right here.

555
00:42:02,460 --> 00:42:04,220
I'm right here,
and I have total confidence in you.

556
00:42:18,430 --> 00:42:19,340
I do, too.

557
00:42:19,850 --> 00:42:20,640
Me too.

558
00:42:21,080 --> 00:42:22,470
Me three.

559
00:42:23,870 --> 00:42:24,710
I also trust you.

560
00:42:25,310 --> 00:42:26,200
- So do we.
- So do we.

561
00:42:42,660 --> 00:42:44,320
Forget everyone else...

562
00:42:44,640 --> 00:42:46,120
and just be my Player Two.

563
00:42:58,890 --> 00:43:01,050
Blue Viper is looking to dive
and pick off Derya first.

564
00:43:01,080 --> 00:43:02,840
In a three-on-one like this,
he's unlikely to survive.

565
00:43:04,740 --> 00:43:07,030
Dive in! Now, go for it.

566
00:43:14,980 --> 00:43:16,390
What a play!

567
00:43:16,420 --> 00:43:17,990
- Hey, fall back!
- He dodged and countered with a single burst.

568
00:43:18,010 --> 00:43:18,830
They're totally scattered!

569
00:43:18,850 --> 00:43:21,200
And now Blue Viper
is forced into a long retreat.

570
00:43:24,650 --> 00:43:25,890
Great job, Soh.

571
00:43:25,970 --> 00:43:28,520
Yeah, push it! This is our chance.

572
00:43:28,910 --> 00:43:30,840
Play it safe. Fall back for now.

573
00:43:30,860 --> 00:43:32,410
Can we counter?

574
00:43:32,440 --> 00:43:33,770
Fall back. It's no good.

575
00:43:33,790 --> 00:43:34,590
Don't. Let's just retreat.

576
00:43:34,610 --> 00:43:35,450
Fall back.

577
00:43:35,880 --> 00:43:38,200
Whoa, this is the Derya we all know!

578
00:43:38,220 --> 00:43:41,360
If you think he can't perform
without the bear head,

579
00:43:41,620 --> 00:43:42,910
well, think again.

580
00:43:43,360 --> 00:43:44,720
- Yeah, almost there.
- Just a little bit more.

581
00:43:44,860 --> 00:43:45,880
Push, push!

582
00:43:46,080 --> 00:43:47,910
- Hey, hey!
- Come on, let's go!

583
00:43:48,000 --> 00:43:49,650
The creeps are here!

584
00:43:49,730 --> 00:43:50,650
Let's end the game!

585
00:43:50,660 --> 00:43:51,500
With the creeps pushing in,

586
00:43:51,520 --> 00:43:53,750
will B.S. Brothers
be able to close it out?

587
00:43:53,800 --> 00:43:55,730
And...

588
00:43:55,950 --> 00:43:57,190
Sh*t! Where are you going?

589
00:43:57,220 --> 00:43:58,820
- Defend the base!
- I'm heading back.

590
00:43:58,840 --> 00:44:00,560
- Hang on, I'm on my way.
- Hurry up, damn it!

591
00:44:19,070 --> 00:44:23,710
And the first game
goes to B.S. Brothers!

592
00:44:23,740 --> 00:44:25,200
What on earth just happened?

593
00:44:25,350 --> 00:44:27,960
We've got the first game!

594
00:44:34,440 --> 00:44:35,340
Sh*t.

595
00:44:35,960 --> 00:44:36,940
I couldn't escape.

596
00:44:37,790 --> 00:44:38,770
Wait for Preaw.

597
00:44:39,350 --> 00:44:40,430
Get the Dark Slayer!

598
00:44:42,450 --> 00:44:44,530
- On it.
- Get in here!

599
00:44:45,090 --> 00:44:46,270
Hey, they're invading our jungle.

600
00:44:50,210 --> 00:44:52,210
Fall back, then. Don't force it.

601
00:44:52,240 --> 00:44:53,380
Don't do it.

602
00:45:26,270 --> 00:45:28,010
- Go for it! I've got this.
- Dive in!

603
00:45:28,030 --> 00:45:29,220
- I've got it.
- I'm taking care of it.

604
00:45:30,210 --> 00:45:30,910
Tank for me.

605
00:45:31,620 --> 00:45:33,340
P'Three, help me out!

606
00:45:33,540 --> 00:45:34,300
Can we fall back in time?

607
00:46:00,460 --> 00:46:02,270
It's alright. Let's go again.

608
00:46:02,510 --> 00:46:05,010
- Yeah, try again.
- Do it again.

609
00:46:05,040 --> 00:46:05,780
Let's go again!

610
00:46:12,100 --> 00:46:13,020
Wait for Preaw to respawn.

611
00:47:09,090 --> 00:47:11,320
Man, looks like another bad call

612
00:47:11,340 --> 00:47:12,830
from ten10 right there.

613
00:47:12,830 --> 00:47:14,770
He's being too aggressive,
and it's costing him.

614
00:47:14,790 --> 00:47:16,170
He's really off his game today.

615
00:47:16,190 --> 00:47:19,100
He's usually better. He's putting
too much pressure on himself.

616
00:47:19,120 --> 00:47:20,530
(The Red Team's tower has been destroyed)
Dive in! Go, go.

617
00:47:21,660 --> 00:47:23,820
- Let's end this!
- End it!

618
00:47:28,440 --> 00:47:31,420
Finish them!

619
00:47:31,710 --> 00:47:33,070
Just like that.

620
00:47:33,630 --> 00:47:35,850
Blue Viper isn't all that after all!

621
00:47:36,040 --> 00:47:39,180
And in the sixth game,
B.S. Brothers took the win,

622
00:47:39,200 --> 00:47:41,540
tying it up at 3-3!

623
00:47:41,570 --> 00:47:43,540
Wow, it's a dead heat.

624
00:47:44,220 --> 00:47:45,120
You pr*ck!

625
00:47:45,210 --> 00:47:46,110
You messed up again.

626
00:47:46,190 --> 00:47:47,190
What the hell did I do?

627
00:47:47,580 --> 00:47:48,760
What kind of sh*tty play was that?

628
00:47:48,790 --> 00:47:49,600
Split pushing all by yourself,

629
00:47:49,620 --> 00:47:51,370
and you couldn't even
break the tower, dammit.

630
00:47:51,370 --> 00:47:52,530
And why didn't you help me?

631
00:47:53,160 --> 00:47:54,200
Hey, enough!

632
00:47:55,950 --> 00:47:58,300
Sh*t, like you're the only one
who's good.

633
00:48:00,030 --> 00:48:01,490
You'll see, Ten.

634
00:48:04,060 --> 00:48:04,780
And finally,

635
00:48:04,800 --> 00:48:06,950
we've reached the ultimate conclusion.

636
00:48:06,970 --> 00:48:08,520
This is the seventh game.

637
00:48:08,630 --> 00:48:14,480
Most importantly, whoever wins this
will be the RPL Summer 2026 champion.

638
00:48:26,480 --> 00:48:28,590
(Abyssal Dragon has been defeated)

639
00:48:30,810 --> 00:48:33,020
That's nice! Keep it going!

640
00:48:33,510 --> 00:48:35,430
- Dammit!
- I'm on my way!

641
00:48:36,200 --> 00:48:37,930
Three up top! Group top!

642
00:48:38,100 --> 00:48:39,700
Yeah, I'm going!

643
00:48:40,230 --> 00:48:41,630
Their Dark Slayer Laner
is in our jungle.

644
00:48:43,470 --> 00:48:45,780
Looks like Blue Viper
wants to end this quickly.

645
00:48:45,800 --> 00:48:47,290
They're all rotating top.

646
00:48:47,320 --> 00:48:49,540
They're definitely gunning for JJack.

647
00:48:49,590 --> 00:48:51,500
They're planning to pressure this lane
all the way.

648
00:48:53,830 --> 00:48:55,140
Keep pushing! Come on!

649
00:48:58,510 --> 00:48:59,850
(The Blue Team's tower
has been destroyed)

650
00:49:01,350 --> 00:49:03,250
Ten, you're low! Recall already!

651
00:49:03,280 --> 00:49:03,970
No retreat.

652
00:49:04,200 --> 00:49:05,700
We can end this. Follow me.

653
00:49:05,990 --> 00:49:07,720
Sh*t, they're unstoppable!

654
00:49:08,410 --> 00:49:09,390
Ladies and gentlemen,

655
00:49:09,410 --> 00:49:11,520
it looks like
the situation for B.S. Brothers

656
00:49:11,560 --> 00:49:13,350
is far from easy now.

657
00:49:13,620 --> 00:49:16,100
And it seems like making a comeback

658
00:49:16,110 --> 00:49:18,310
with no towers left like this

659
00:49:18,430 --> 00:49:19,640
is almost impossible.

660
00:49:19,670 --> 00:49:22,340
In other words, the other team's
chances of losing are slim to none.

661
00:49:24,700 --> 00:49:25,800
Jack, target the backline!

662
00:49:26,220 --> 00:49:27,870
- On it.
- Yeah.

663
00:49:31,060 --> 00:49:33,330
Hey, they're all in! They're all in!

664
00:49:33,360 --> 00:49:34,800
- Help me out!
- Whoa!

665
00:49:39,610 --> 00:49:41,180
Whoa! A hellish counter-combo.

666
00:49:41,220 --> 00:49:43,360
That was a sharp Quad Kill!

667
00:49:43,390 --> 00:49:45,500
Only PEEM remains!

668
00:49:45,530 --> 00:49:48,240
Counter-push! Push now!

669
00:49:49,030 --> 00:49:50,200
Stay calm.

670
00:49:50,480 --> 00:49:51,500
Everyone, stay calm.

671
00:49:53,530 --> 00:49:54,860
Guys, calm down.

672
00:49:54,900 --> 00:49:55,740
Wait, wait!

673
00:49:55,760 --> 00:49:57,830
Hey, what is PEEM doing?

674
00:49:57,900 --> 00:49:59,370
I've got it! Told you I've got this.

675
00:49:59,470 --> 00:50:01,820
We're in time!
Defend! Just hold them off.

676
00:50:02,560 --> 00:50:04,030
(Deploying Super Creeps)

677
00:50:05,840 --> 00:50:07,060
No, no, no!

678
00:50:07,090 --> 00:50:09,180
Which is gonna break first,
their base or my head?

679
00:50:09,210 --> 00:50:11,060
Whose base is going to break first?

680
00:50:46,180 --> 00:50:49,830
Whoa, they've finally won
the final game.

681
00:50:49,860 --> 00:50:52,830
Before my voice gave out,
the enemy base went down first.

682
00:50:52,860 --> 00:50:54,680
And it ends with a victory
for Blue Viper.

683
00:50:54,750 --> 00:50:55,860
That was absolutely impressive.

684
00:51:26,920 --> 00:51:27,680
Sh*t,

685
00:51:28,130 --> 00:51:29,310
that was so damn fun.

686
00:51:30,200 --> 00:51:30,860
Exactly!

687
00:51:31,090 --> 00:51:32,400
I'm not even sad.

688
00:51:33,060 --> 00:51:35,660
Coming this far
is already a massive win for us!

689
00:51:35,890 --> 00:51:37,690
To hell with what anyone else thinks.

690
00:51:37,790 --> 00:51:39,400
We f*cking did our best.

691
00:51:40,310 --> 00:51:42,020
We really gave it our all.

692
00:51:46,530 --> 00:51:49,960
Playing with you guys was fun as hell.

693
00:51:51,770 --> 00:51:53,490
I'm sorry, everyone.

694
00:51:53,510 --> 00:51:55,480
I messed up several times today.

695
00:51:56,960 --> 00:51:58,170
You don't need to be sorry.

696
00:51:59,630 --> 00:52:00,520
Yeah.

697
00:52:00,730 --> 00:52:02,680
Just the fact
that you took off that bear head

698
00:52:02,910 --> 00:52:04,240
means we've already won.

699
00:52:08,590 --> 00:52:10,390
You're the absolute best to me.

700
00:52:18,370 --> 00:52:19,230
Well done.

701
00:52:20,900 --> 00:52:22,330
You guys did a great job.

702
00:52:24,080 --> 00:52:25,310
Can I give them a hug?

703
00:52:25,870 --> 00:52:26,870
Dammit.

704
00:52:27,170 --> 00:52:28,410
That's how you do it!

705
00:52:29,520 --> 00:52:30,320
B.S. ...

706
00:52:30,380 --> 00:52:31,340
- Brothers!
- Brothers!

707
00:52:31,360 --> 00:52:32,050
B.S. ...

708
00:52:32,080 --> 00:52:32,950
- Brothers!
- Brothers!

709
00:52:32,970 --> 00:52:33,650
B.S. ...

710
00:52:33,680 --> 00:52:34,530
- Brothers!
- Brothers!

711
00:52:34,550 --> 00:52:35,140
B.S. ...

712
00:52:35,160 --> 00:52:36,060
- Brothers!
- Brothers!

713
00:52:39,090 --> 00:52:40,290
Let's go!

714
00:52:40,790 --> 00:52:41,620
Let's go!

715
00:52:55,450 --> 00:52:56,690
Thank you.

716
00:52:59,170 --> 00:53:00,110
Thank you.

717
00:53:00,130 --> 00:53:02,220
Thank you. Thank you so much.

718
00:53:03,830 --> 00:53:04,730
Hello, everyone.

719
00:53:15,370 --> 00:53:16,780
- I'm heading out first.
- What?

720
00:53:18,740 --> 00:53:19,720
Where is he going?

721
00:53:23,460 --> 00:53:25,180
Luckily, Peem carried the team.

722
00:53:26,170 --> 00:53:27,410
Otherwise, the championship
would've slipped away.

723
00:53:30,290 --> 00:53:31,620
You're just a sub.

724
00:53:33,470 --> 00:53:34,500
Don't get too cocky.

725
00:53:47,050 --> 00:53:48,010
Are you here to kick me
while I'm down?

726
00:53:50,450 --> 00:53:52,420
If you're here to talk about
that f*cking bear head,

727
00:53:52,550 --> 00:53:53,820
just leave.

728
00:53:54,170 --> 00:53:55,140
I don't want to talk about it.

729
00:53:55,520 --> 00:53:57,240
I actually believed you
about that bear head.

730
00:53:58,370 --> 00:53:59,480
That's all you came to say?

731
00:54:00,480 --> 00:54:01,100
Huh?

732
00:54:02,400 --> 00:54:03,040
No.

733
00:54:04,110 --> 00:54:05,500
Actually, I came to say...

734
00:54:06,540 --> 00:54:07,520
congratulations.

735
00:54:10,280 --> 00:54:11,960
If you're only saying that to be polite,

736
00:54:12,440 --> 00:54:13,580
piss off.

737
00:54:13,850 --> 00:54:14,920
That's not what I'm doing.

738
00:54:15,160 --> 00:54:16,180
I really mean it.

739
00:54:16,710 --> 00:54:17,730
The game is over,

740
00:54:18,350 --> 00:54:20,090
and so is our status as rivals.

741
00:54:21,550 --> 00:54:23,820
I just wanted
to congratulate you, buddy.

742
00:54:34,650 --> 00:54:35,860
About what you told me...

743
00:54:37,140 --> 00:54:38,400
that when the tournament is over...

744
00:54:39,420 --> 00:54:40,790
we'd go back to being friends.

745
00:54:42,600 --> 00:54:43,820
Don't you forget that.

746
00:55:27,950 --> 00:55:29,420
Laem, over here!

747
00:55:29,440 --> 00:55:30,550
Oh, I see.

748
00:55:36,990 --> 00:55:38,730
It wasn't me! That wasn't me.

749
00:55:45,830 --> 00:55:46,600
Don't stop yet.

750
00:55:47,010 --> 00:55:48,290
Make some more noise!

751
00:56:00,510 --> 00:56:01,250
Is this it?

752
00:56:01,610 --> 00:56:04,160
Is this what you said
you'd prove to me and your mom?

753
00:56:12,390 --> 00:56:13,690
I'm home.

754
00:56:14,490 --> 00:56:16,900
How was it, son? Have you eaten yet?

755
00:56:17,390 --> 00:56:18,400
Go ahead, Mom.

756
00:56:20,970 --> 00:56:23,300
And how is your brother doing?

757
00:56:23,900 --> 00:56:26,060
Well, he won his match today.

758
00:56:26,230 --> 00:56:27,720
He should be in the final tomorrow.

759
00:56:28,420 --> 00:56:30,920
I meant his life.

760
00:56:31,010 --> 00:56:33,820
How has he been lately?
Is he doing okay?

761
00:56:34,900 --> 00:56:35,940
He's fine.

762
00:56:36,170 --> 00:56:39,540
Whether he's fine or not,
he's making six figures a month.

763
00:56:42,080 --> 00:56:44,020
He has millions of followers, you know.

764
00:56:44,540 --> 00:56:46,060
You should check it out, Mom, Dad.

765
00:56:50,200 --> 00:56:52,100
Even though he's never said it,

766
00:56:53,590 --> 00:56:55,880
he really wants both of you
to watch him compete.

767
00:56:59,020 --> 00:57:01,180
I'm going to get some rest now.

768
00:57:02,150 --> 00:57:03,790
- Go ahead, son.
- Okay.

769
00:57:12,010 --> 00:57:14,040
(A lot of you have been asking me,)

770
00:57:14,160 --> 00:57:15,580
("Why do you even compete?")

771
00:57:15,900 --> 00:57:17,890
(Let me tell you
what my ultimate dream is.)

772
00:57:18,140 --> 00:57:19,290
It's not about
the hundreds of thousands,

773
00:57:19,350 --> 00:57:20,480
or the millions,

774
00:57:20,620 --> 00:57:22,440
or any of those view counts.

775
00:57:22,470 --> 00:57:23,310
Not at all.

776
00:57:24,230 --> 00:57:26,780
(It's about getting a trophy...)

777
00:57:27,330 --> 00:57:28,480
(to show off to my parents.)

778
00:57:29,830 --> 00:57:33,020
(I just want to tell them,
"Look at your son,)

779
00:57:33,420 --> 00:57:35,470
(the one who used to just
play games all day long.")

780
00:57:36,200 --> 00:57:38,180
("He's a pro player now.")

781
00:57:39,090 --> 00:57:42,180
(He's so good
he even became a national champion.)

782
00:57:43,720 --> 00:57:45,930
(I just want them to be proud,)

783
00:57:47,800 --> 00:57:50,830
so they can finally brag about me.

784
00:57:53,660 --> 00:57:56,160
Wanna watch on the big screen?
I'll turn it on for you.

785
00:57:57,400 --> 00:57:58,260
No need.

786
00:58:00,820 --> 00:58:02,140
If I watch on the big screen,

787
00:58:02,560 --> 00:58:04,340
I won't be able to send him donuts.

788
00:58:08,230 --> 00:58:08,900
Look,

789
00:58:09,230 --> 00:58:10,700
it's not a donut.

790
00:58:11,020 --> 00:58:13,110
It's called donating, honey.

791
00:58:40,050 --> 00:58:42,880
And that trophy you said
you'd bring home for us...

792
00:58:43,810 --> 00:58:45,150
Whenever you get it,

793
